:: OC Leo Modeling Quest [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 30>>
You stand outside the address listed on the modeling job application. It is a small building shoved between a card shop and a ninja-themed noodle place. The entertainment district tends to have a large variety of stuff, acting as something of a large touristy area that is less structured than the food and shopping district. But that’s also what makes it fun for visitors and locals alike. This building is pretty plain by comparison, grey brick without any large sign or display, simply a plaque with the name of the modeling company next to the door. It looks like it may be rather new, which would explain the simple design, though you get a little nervous.

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

You wonder if you should knock on the plain white door but thankfully spot another boy around your age walking in with his mother. You follow behind, moving down a small hallway to a counter where you sign in. When asked if a parent is with you, you’re a little worried, but it doesn’t seem to be a requirement. You are then moved to a waiting room where about 8-9 other boys sit. Some alone, some with a friend, and a few with their parents. You quickly piece together that this isn’t just an open gig, but an audition. <span style="Color:Yellow">This makes you EXTREMELY nervous as you take a seat and anxiously wait for your name to be called.</span> <br>
<br>
You were handed a small pamphlet when you signed in which details what you’re expected to do. It explains that Boy Barn wants some locals to model with the hired professional model to give the photos some Opal City charm. There are a few age groups listed, each talking about the vibe they want for that pair. 5-9 year olds need a <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“little brother”</span> vibe. Cute or bratty. Meanwhile your age group, 10+, will be expected to give off a <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“best friend”</span> vibe with the professional actor. The gist of it is that chemistry with this model is important. Each audition is really just a test of that. They’ll see how you look next to him and answer a few questions. The director and model will pick some that they like to do a screen test, modeling a few clothes. Those that pass this will be given the gig. <br>
<br>
You note the lack of explanation on pay, just like the job posting. It mentions it is a paid gig, but nothing about the amount or what even will be required. Body type, appearance, nothing like that is listed. Maybe the company doesn’t want to seem shallow? Or maybe they don’t know what they want? You read the back, which lists some information about the modeling agency. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“True Blue Modeling.”</span> The pamphlet reads, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The agency specializes in providing models for products ranging from clothes to adverts to commercials. Our models focus on boys from ages 3 all the way to 60+! True Blue Modeling is the go-to for many brands nationwide with a large network of models along with a robust recruitment platform for discovering local and unknown boys to spice up any product!”</span> It is clearly a fluff piece, though the company seems to be rather large. Though one thing that catches your eye is that the pamphlet has three logos on it. One is True Blue Modeling, which makes sense, along with Boy Barn. But the third logo looks a little strange. You don’t think you’ve seen it before. It almost looks like- <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name $Player.LastName</span>!”</span> A young woman calls out. The mention of your full name causes you to snap up to your feet, caught off guard. The woman sees you stand and smiles. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“They will see you now.”</span> <span style="Color:Yellow">You nod, quickly fixing your hair as you hurry over through the small yet intimidating blue door.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    You walk into the audition room; it looks exactly like they do on T.V. A long desk where three people sit, a large area for you to stand, and a camera facing directly at you. You notice a pair of doors on your right with signs on them, though they are too far to see. Of the three people at the desk, one is a tired woman hastily writing things down in a notepad. Another is a larger gentleman eating a sandwich. The third is an older man that looks like what you’d imagine a Hollywood producer looked like. Black jacket, greying hair, shades, but he also has an aura of cheapness. Like he’s trying to appear wealthier than he actually is. <br>

    /* PC: Frown, Blush1 */

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alrighty! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.LastName</span>! Our last audition for today. We’ve already gotten some people down, but we still have spots to fill! So do your best and let’s rock this show!”</span> His voice only adds to your earlier impression. He sounds energetic and hype, though there is an underlying level of exhaustion and nervousness. You’re unsure if going last is a good of bad thing. The larger man doesn’t pay attention, so focused on his sandwich, while the woman yawns and begins to go over her notes. <span style="Color:Yellow">So, in this case, going last is bad. Seems all three of them are worn out from their earlier auditions. Getting their attention may not be easy.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Where’s <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span>? <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span>, my boy, are you ready? One last one!”</span> The producer calls out towards the twin doors. A moment later, a voice answers and a familiar boy steps out. <br>
    <br>
    The boy has miscolored eyes, brown hair, and is a little chubby. It takes you maybe a second or two to suddenly realize you’ve seen this boy before. Not in person, but on Gabe’s computer screen! <span style="Color:Pink">It’s <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo Page</span>, that naughty streamer you watched recently! The one who-!</span> <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "OC Leo",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey there!”</span> Your recognition must read on your face. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span>, previously looking a little tired himself, lights up as he sees you. A smirk on his face as he walks over, looking you up and down before smiling wider. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Not bad! I think he definitely has the look we’re looking for, at least from what I can see.”</span> As he gets closer, you can’t help but say his name under your breath, looking for some kind of confirmation that he is who you think. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, so you’ve heard of me? Always nice to meet a fan. You watch my streams or-?”</span> <span style="Color:Pink">Your blush is all the answer he needs.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Wait! You’re right, that looks pretty good!”</span> The producer suddenly leans forward, finding your blush and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span>’s smirk enduring. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yes, I think I can see the dynamic! Get the camera going, let’s see how they look together. Just act natural! Pretend we’re not here!”</span> <span style="Color:Pink">You get more nervous as the camera is turned towards you, its large lens feeling like it can see into your soul.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Don’t be nervous.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span> laughs, noticing your worry, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s just so they have something to give the director. We just have to chat for a moment, ignore them and the camera.”</span> He gives you a reassuring smile before asking you some basic questions to get the conversation going. You try to ponder how you should act. <br>
    <br>
    [[Act shy|OC Leo Modeling Quest Shy]]<br>
    [[Act confident|OC Leo Modeling Quest Confident]]<br>
    <<requiresTrait "Athletic" "Only if you can participate<br>">>
        <<goto"OC Leo Modeling Quest Lewd">>
    <</requiresTrait>>
<</linkreplace>>

:: OC Leo Modeling Quest Shy [nobr]

<span style="Color:Pink">You act a bit shy for the camera, or maybe you are just shy. The point is, you stand a little awkwardly, move a little stiffly, and a tiny blush of pink is constant on your face. But <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span> seems to be able to perfectly play off of this, acting as the more confident, daring member of your duo and even stages some rather adorable poses.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yes, yes! You two look perfect together!”</span> The producer laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Your dynamic is already so clear, so pure! The quiet nervous boy brought out of his shell and into daring adventures by his much more rebellious friend! It’s perfect!”</span> Both of the other two at the table nod along with the producer as he jumps to his feet. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What do you think, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span>?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I think he’ll work well. We don’t have this dynamic yet and it would work well for some shoots.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span> pauses for a moment, thinking, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Why don’t we try some sleepover poses, to send to the director? I think he’d look great in those.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span> gives you a smile as the producer claps his hands together in agreement. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color:Pink">You are then both brought out a pair of pajamas. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Leo</span> is given a rather more mature pair of pajama bottoms that sit loosely on him, pulled down just enough to reveal the waistband of his underwear, the brand name displayed prominently. You, meanwhile, get stuck with a childish onesie, your role as the more ‘childish’ boy set in stone as you walk out of the changing room in the slightly tight pajamas.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
